# hui DARK FORCE STYLE — the NATIVE-COMPARABLE rig (14z-69, the item
# NEXT_SESSION opened on). Runs UNCHANGED on native vsav2 and on a
# variant-id build, so ours-vs-native is one diff at the same phase.
#
# THE BLOCKER THAT WAS NOT ONE: 14z-68j recorded "the early-window id
# poke does NOT force him on vsav2". That was replay 61 (a win-screen
# replay whose input timing is authored for OUR wheel). The replay-80
# early-window poke flow DOES reach him natively — measured this
# session on replay 82: char id +0x382 = 0x10 and seq 0x0A at the DF
# frame on BOTH games. No vs2 cursor path and no savestate is needed.
#
# BOTH SIDES ARE POKED so the two legs differ only in the GAME:
#   P1 $FF8782 = 0x10 (Huitzil, native id on both)
#   P2 $FF8B82 = 0x03 (Victor — id 0x03 on vsav AND vsav2, verified
#                      by pick in docs/atlas/character_tables.md)
# without the P2 poke the cursor path R,R lands on different
# characters on the two wheels and the sprite lists are not comparable.
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03"
#
# WHY AIR DASH: the maintainer's repro is "1 stock, HP+HK, then move —
# air dash shows it best". Replay 82 only WALKS, and at its walk phase
# ours and native are equivalent (measured 14z-69: pal-0x0A counts,
# x-spans and palette row 0x0A all track native modulo a ~2-frame
# skew). So replay 82 cannot see this symptom; this replay adds the
# motion that does.
#
# THE CONTROL IS INSIDE THE REPLAY: the SAME air dash is performed
# before DF (f3160) and twice during it (f3320, f3450), with the 79
# air-dash timing measured good on both games. Any DF style shows up
# as the pre/post difference, and native-vs-ours as the cross-leg one.
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# control air dash, DF NOT yet active (replay 79 timing: jump f3160 is
# the measured-good accept frame; f3060 jumps are eaten on both games)
3160-3162 p1=U
3175-3177 p1=R
3181-3183 p1=R
# activate Dark Force (LP+LK; same button pair as replay 82)
3260-3263 p1=14
# DF air dash #1
3320-3322 p1=U
3335-3337 p1=R
3341-3343 p1=R
# DF air dash #2
3450-3452 p1=U
3465-3467 p1=R
3471-3473 p1=R
# DF walk (the replay-82 phase, kept so both motions are in one rig)
3550-3650 p1=R
3800 wait
